idate.py`)\n- The fallback path used to return the first `*.dist-info/METADATA` in the zip. Vendored packages could win that match.\n- The expected path is now built from the wheel filename, as the issue suggests. A new helper, `_wheel_metadata_path()`, takes the URL path's basename and splits off the name and version. Both are safe to split on `-` because they can't contain it, even when an optional build tag is present.\n- If that exact path is missing, it raises `ValueError` naming the expected path, rather than falling back to a vendored file.\n- The PEP 658 `.metadata` endpoint path is unchanged.\n\n**The tests** (`tests/test_pep658_support.py`)\n- `test_get_metadata_ignores_vendored_dist_info`: the wheel has a vendored `vendored_pkg-2.0.0.dist-info` listed before the real one. The result must be the wheel's own metadata.\n- `test_get_metadata_raises_when_wheel_dist_info_missing`: the wheel contains only a vendored dist-info, so the call must raise.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- I used the filename-derived path (the issue's \"better\" option) rather than scanning only root-level `.dist-info` directories. Both are satisfied by this change.\n- I did not use `packaging.utils.parse_wheel_filename`. It returns a canonicalized name, but the dist-info directory uses the escaped name from the filename, so the raw split is the safer choice.\n\n**Not run:** `mypy` and `ruff` aren't installed in `.venv`, so I couldn't run the file-scoped type check and lint that the project guidelines ask for. The full test suite was not run either.", "ttft_ms": 1307, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 24114, "uuid": "5bad583b-e2ac-49ca-a966-647cda2f883f", "ttft_stream_ms": 788, "time_to_request_ms": 136, "first_content_frame_ms": 788, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-10-09T15:35:10.801Z"}